Finding: Worker rechecked the frozen Handoff policy at the bounded physical-send callback, but did not check the channel `CredentialUseLease` against that fresh trusted-time sample. A queued task could therefore reach Producer after the credential lease expired.

Change: `CredentialUseLease.requireActiveAt` requires `trustedTime.earliestEpochMs >= issuedAt.latestEpochMs` and `trustedTime.latestEpochMs < validUntilEpochMs`. `WorkerPhysicalPublishExecutor.requireFrozenHandoffLease` reuses that value-level check at both the preflight and final Producer-ownership boundary. The canonical lease encoding is unchanged.

